{"availability":"available","full":"mazin-musleh/NDS-vanilla","name":"NDS-vanilla","description":"An open-source vanilla implementation of Saudi Arabia's National Design System — RTL/LTR native, plain HTML/CSS/JS, zero runtime dependencies.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":19,"forks":8,"created":"2025-08-16T19:58:01Z","updated":"2026-10-03T21:13:06Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://mazin-musleh.github.io/NDS-vanilla","topics":["accessibility","design-system","government","jekyll","national-design-system","nds","open-source","platform-code","platformscode","rtl","saudi-arabia","scss"],"demo":"https://mazin-musleh.github.io/NDS-vanilla/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:35.661Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:35.661Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:35.661Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T06:51:35.661Z","stars":19,"forks":8}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The Saudi Digital Government Authority (DGA) publishes its design specifications as Figma files. Its own code is a React and Storybook component library.","NDS-vanilla is an independent build of the same design system in plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Plain web code works in any stack: static sites, server-rendered pages, or apps built with React or another framework. It brings no framework or dependencies of its own.","Accessibility: Components are tested by hand against WCAG 2.1 AA. An automated audit with axe-core and screen readers is planned. Known gaps are tracked in issues labeled accessibility."],"features":["Framework-free. Plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, with zero runtime dependencies.","More than components. A layout system, page templates, live documentation, and a 4-tier design-token system (palette, primitives, semantic, component).","DGA page templates. Common government service pages as working code, built on the DGA tokens, typography, spacing, and interaction patterns.","Fast.